1
00:00:00,414 --> 00:00:01,454
(Sheldon:)Thank you, Kripke...

2
00:00:01,624 --> 00:00:05,334
(Sheldon:)...for depriving me of the opportunity
to share my news with my friends.

3
00:00:05,502 --> 00:00:07,422
(Sheldon:)My pleasure.

4
00:00:07,588 --> 00:00:11,508
-My thank-you was not sincere.
-But my pleasure is.

5
00:00:12,426 --> 00:00:13,756
(Kripke:)Let me ask you a question.

6
00:00:13,928 --> 00:00:16,308
(Kripke:)At what point
did National Public Radio...

7
00:00:16,472 --> 00:00:20,182
...have to start scraping the bottom
of the barrel for its guests?

8
00:00:20,392 --> 00:00:22,982
Eeh-eeh. Don't answer. It's rhetorical.

9
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,980
Well, why are you such a stupidhead?

10
00:00:27,441 --> 00:00:29,691
(Sheldon:)That is also rhetorical.

11
00:00:31,028 --> 00:00:33,448
(Sheldon:)I'm sorry you had to hear that.

12
00:00:33,614 --> 00:00:35,494
Are you really gonna be on NPR?

13
00:00:35,658 --> 00:00:38,288
(Sheldon:)Yes, they're interviewing me by phone
from my office...

14
00:00:38,452 --> 00:00:42,792
(Sheldon:)...regarding the recent so-called discovery
of magnetic monopoles in spin ices.

15
00:00:42,957 --> 00:00:47,127
(Sheldon:)It's pledge week, and they're trying
to goose the ratings with controversy.

16
00:00:48,128 --> 00:00:51,798
(Leonard:)-Very cool. Congratulations.
-Thank you. My mother is very excited.

17
00:00:51,966 --> 00:00:54,466
(Sheldon:)She's convening her Bible study group
to listen in...

18
00:00:54,635 --> 00:00:58,025
(Sheldon:)...and then pray for my soul.

